<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Wayna Daga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1543</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Wayna Daga · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-adal-war">Ethiopian–Adal War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Wayna Daga was fought on 21 February 1543 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-highlands">Ethiopian highlands</a>, where Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galawdewos">Galawdewos</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a>, aided by Portuguese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musketeers</a>, defeated and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Ghazi</a>, known as Ahmad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Gran</a>. The Portuguese contingent had arrived under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cristovao-da-gama">Cristóvão da Gama</a>. The battle ended the Adalite conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and began the decline of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> as a military power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-wayna-daga.jpg" alt="Battle of Wayna Daga" width="320" height="111" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kegneketa Jemlieri Hailu of Gondar (fl.1900) · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_fall_and_death_of_Ahmad_Gragn.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
